    "description": "# napari-emaki\n\n\u30b7\u30fc\u30c0\u30f3\u30b9\uff08Seedance\uff092.5 \u3068 2.0 \u3092\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e\u306e\u307e\u307e\u4f7f\u3048\u307e\u3059\u3002\u4e00\u6587\u3084\u5199\u771f\u304b\u3089 1 \u672c\u6700\u9577 30 \u79d2\u306e AI \u52d5\u753b\u3092\u751f\u6210\u3067\u304d\u3001480p\u301c1080p\u30fb\u97f3\u58f0\u3064\u304d\u306b\u5bfe\u5fdc\u3002\u767b\u9332\u3059\u308b\u3060\u3051\u3067\u7121\u6599\u30af\u30ec\u30b8\u30c3\u30c8\u304c\u3064\u304d\u3001\u6d88\u8cbb\u3059\u308b\u30af\u30ec\u30b8\u30c3\u30c8\u306f\u751f\u6210\u524d\u306b\u5fc5\u305a\u8868\u793a\u3055\u308c\u307e\u3059\u3002\n\nA [napari](https://napari.org/) plugin for [Emaki (emaki.ai)](https://emaki.ai/) that generates [Seedance 2.5](https://emaki.ai/seedance-2-5) and [Seedance 2.0](https://emaki.ai/seedance-2) AI video clips and loads the decoded MP4 frames directly as a time-series RGB image layer.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install napari-emaki\n```\n\nCreate an API key at [emaki.ai/settings/apikeys](https://emaki.ai/settings/apikeys) and set `EMAKI_API_KEY` (or enter it in the widget).\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open napari and choose **Plugins \u2192 Emaki Seedance AI Video**.\n2. Enter a Japanese or English prompt, select a model (`seedance_2_5`, `seedance_2`, `seedance_2_fast`, `seedance_2_mini`, `minimax_h3`, or `veo_3_1`), duration, and aspect ratio.\n3. Click **Generate** to append the rendered video frames as an RGB image stack layer.\n\n## Links\n\n- [Emaki \u2014 \u30b7\u30fc\u30c0\u30f3\u30b9 AI \u52d5\u753b\u751f\u6210](https://emaki.ai/)\n- [Seedance 2.5 (\u30b7\u30fc\u30c0\u30f3\u30b9 2.5)](https://emaki.ai/seedance-2-5)\n- [Image to Video AI (\u753b\u50cf\u304b\u3089\u52d5\u753b)](https://emaki.ai/image-to-video)\n- [Video Upscaler (AI \u52d5\u753b\u9ad8\u753b\u8cea\u5316)](https://emaki.ai/video-upscaler)\n- [Pricing & JPY Credit Packs](https://emaki.ai/pricing)\n- [API Documentation](https://emaki.readthedocs.io/en/latest/)\n\nMIT licensed.\n",
